sxml - check, validate, query and transform XML documents

Usage: sxml [--version] COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]

sxml checks XML 1.0 and 1.1 documents, validates them against DTDs
and XSD 1.1 schemas, evaluates XPath 4.0 expressions and XQuery 4.0
queries, and runs XSLT 4.0 stylesheets. Results go to standard
output, errors to standard error. Documents, schemas and modules are
read from local files; sxml never uses the network. A FILE operand
of - reads standard input.

Exit status: 0 on success; 1 when the operation fails (a document
is not well-formed or not valid, a query or stylesheet raises an
error); 2 for a usage error; 3 when a file cannot be read or
written; 4 for an internal error or an exceeded limit.

Commands:
  help       Show help for the program or for one command
  check      Check that XML documents are well-formed
  serialize  Parse an XML document and write it out again
  transform  Transform a document with an XSLT 4.0 stylesheet
  validate   Validate XML documents against an XSD 1.1 schema
  version    Print the sxml version
  xpath      Evaluate an XPath 4.0 expression
  xquery     Run an XQuery 4.0 query

Options:
  -h, --help     Show this help and exit
      --version  Print the version and exit

Examples:
  sxml check books.xml
  sxml validate --schema=books.xsd books.xml
  sxml xpath --context-item=books.xml '//title/string()'
  sxml xquery --context-item=books.xml titles.xq
  sxml transform list.xsl books.xml

Run 'sxml help COMMAND' for help on one command.
Report bugs at https://github.com/dhamidi/sxml/issues
